From: Nicolin Chen <nicolinc@nvidia.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Jun 2025 23:35:14 -0700
Subject: iommufd: Drop unused ictx in struct iommufd_vdevice
Patch-mainline: v6.17-rc1
Git-commit: 6e235a77219934d24cc356336a811ed19e439765
References: jsc#PED-16989

The core code can always get the ictx pointer via vdev->viommu->ictx, thus
drop this unused one.

Link: https://patch.msgid.link/r/6cbb65e8df433de45b6c3a4bb2c5df09faca8a7c.1749882255.git.nicolinc@nvidia.com
Reviewed-by: Kevin Tian <kevin.tian@intel.com>
Reviewed-by: Jason Gunthorpe <jgg@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Nicolin Chen <nicolinc@nvidia.com>
Reviewed-by: Lu Baolu <baolu.lu@linux.intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Jason Gunthorpe <jgg@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carlos López <clopez@suse.de>
---
 drivers/iommu/iommufd/iommufd_private.h |    1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/iommu/iommufd/iommufd_private.h
+++ b/drivers/iommu/iommufd/iommufd_private.h
@@ -630,7 +630,6 @@ void iommufd_vdevice_destroy(struct iomm
 
 struct iommufd_vdevice {
 	struct iommufd_object obj;
-	struct iommufd_ctx *ictx;
 	struct iommufd_viommu *viommu;
 	struct device *dev;
 	u64 id; /* per-vIOMMU virtual ID */
